SUMMARY:Deadline: TBA21-Academy: UNI Weather Commons Working Group Fall 202
 6 (online\, fully funded places)
DESCRIPTION:UNI is TBA21-Academy's para-academic program\; the Fall 2026 te
 rm\, Weather Commons: On the Practice and Politics of Atmospheric Modifica
 tion\, investigates how the atmosphere is being reshaped technically\, pol
 itically and culturally. It spans rainmaking rituals\, cloud seeding\, ant
 i-hail infrastructure\, weather militarization\, atmospheric simulation\, 
 AI forecasting and geoengineering\, and asks: if the atmosphere is a commo
 ns\, who has the right to change the weather? Co-curated by FAST (Eva Fran
 ch i Gilabert and Jose Luis de Vicente) and TBA21-Academy (Eduardo Castill
 o-Vinuesa and Aleksandra Czerniak). THE FUNDED PART\, THE WORKING GROUP: a
 pproximately 12 practitioners from interdisciplinary backgrounds are selec
 ted via international open call for a temporary online research laboratory
  led by researchers and architects Farzin Lotfi-Jam and Boone Mercado. Its
  focus\, Realtime Weather\, has participants critically explore spatial-te
 mporal datasets and models to investigate how the environment is monitored
 \, modeled\, forecast and managed\, using an AI-assisted software developm
 ent framework to build experimental visualizations\, simulations\, interfa
 ces and spatial research outputs. Outcomes are open-ended (presentations\,
  digital tools\, research resources\, prototypes) and feed a shared public
 ation released first on Ocean-Archive.org with a physical edition to follo
 w. COMMITMENT: four online sessions between 2 and 23 November 2026\, 6 to 
 8pm CET\, 100 percent attendance required\, plus roughly 10 hours of indep
 endent work. Participation is free\; all places are fully funded. ALSO ON 
 OFFER: five public online seminar sessions (14 October to 10 November\, 6 
 to 7:30pm CET) with speakers including Sarah Strauss\, Ala Roushan\, Charl
 es Stankievech\, Karolina Sobecka\, Lucia Rebolino\, Luiza Crossman\, Desi
 gn Earth\, Elise Hunchuck\, Marco Ferrari and Manon Simon\; seminar regist
 ration carries a fee\, disclosed in the registration form. TIMELINE: Worki
 ng Group applications close 4 October 2026 via Google Form linked from the
  program page\; acceptance notifications 19 October 2026. Contact: hello@t
 ba21-academy.org.\n\nOrganisation: TBA21-Academy and FAST\nLocation: Onlin
 e (Zoom). International open call.\nAward: All approximately 12 Working Gr
 oup places are fully funded\; participation is free of charge with no fee.
  No cash stipend is advertised. The parallel public seminar series does ch
 arge a registration fee (the amount is only disclosed in the registration 
 form)\, but the Working Group itself costs nothing.\nDuration: Four online
  evening sessions between 2 and 23 November 2026\, 6 to 8pm CET\, plus aro
 und 10 hours of independent work. Part of the wider UNI Weather Commons te
 rm\, 14 October to 23 November 2026.\n\nMore: https://tba21.org/uni-wc?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
